{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/x4r21kru","slideIndex":1,"position":{"left":80.36,"top":216.68,"width":1081.24,"height":89.99},"name":"Text 4","text":"Good food is wasted while nearby communities face shortages. Donors, NGOs and food banks often coordinate through fragmented manual channels, making suitable matches and safe, timely handoffs difficult.","geometry":"rect","style":{"fontSize":26.67,"typeface":"IBM Plex Sans","color":"#000000","alignment":"left"}}
